abstract: >-
  The Social Interaction Cloud (SIC) is a Python framework
  for building social robot and human-AI interaction
  applications. It addresses a common problem in human-robot
  interaction research: a typical study needs a robot to
  simultaneously coordinate sensors, actuators, and external
  AI services such as speech recognition, natural language
  processing, and computer vision, often across multiple
  devices and SDKs that do not natively interoperate.

  SIC lets researchers build applications by connecting
  modular components, sensors, actuators, and services, over
  a Redis-based messaging layer, with ComponentManagers
  handling deployment on distributed hosts and Connectors
  providing a single interface for application scripts.

  The framework supports multiple robot platforms, including
  Pepper, NAO, AlphaMini, and Reachy Mini, integrates with
  external AI APIs, and includes a Model Context Protocol
  (MCP) layer for driving robot components as tools for
  LLM-based agents. Its goal is to let researchers and
  students focus on interaction design and study logic
  rather than reimplementing device drivers,
  message-passing, and multi-user robot access control for
  each new project.
